<title>USA: IBM sells $850 mln in 100-year debt.</title>
<headline>IBM sells $850 mln in 100-year debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from International Business Machines Corp was priced on Tuesday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers Inc</p>
<p>BORROWER: INTERNATIONAL BUSINESS MACHINES CORP</p>
<p>AMT $850 MLN	 COUPON 7.125	MATURITY 12/1/2096</p>
<p>TYPE DEBENTURES    ISS PRICE 98.687  FIRST PAY DATE 6/1/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 7.22 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-A  SPREAD 80 BPS     CALLABLE MAKE-WHOLE CALL</p>
<p>AT 15 BASIS POINTS OVER U.S. TREASURIES</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1662</p>
</text>
